        passage: "Hi, I'm Cansu. My alarm goes off at a quarter past six, but I always press the snooze button once, so I really get up at 6.30. The first thing I do after that is drink a glass of water and open the window. Then I put on my school uniform. After that I check that my bag is packed, because I get it ready the night before. Breakfast comes next, and it is quick: cheese toast and a cup of tea, eaten standing up in the kitchen. Then Dad gives me a lift as far as the market, and I walk the last five minutes to school. My first lesson starts at 8.30. At break time my best friend and I go to the canteen and share a simit. On Mondays and Thursdays I stay after school for volleyball practice. On the other days I do my homework in the library next to the school, because my little brother is too noisy at home. I get back at about six and help Mum with dinner, and we eat together at half past seven. After dinner I watch one episode of a series, then I read for twenty minutes before I turn the light off. Weekends are different: I sleep until nine and go cycling with my cousins.",
