        passage: "Education is changing quickly because of technology. Pupils can understand lessons more easily, get extra practice and improve in the subjects they study. In many countries, interactive whiteboards and online platforms have become common in schools, since they make learning more interesting. Türkiye is following the same path with a national project, Digital Transformation in Education, designed for learners and teachers alike. On its online platforms, experts have prepared the lessons and materials. A student can watch videos, complete exercises and move forward at a speed that suits them, so weak points are easy to spot and can be improved one at a time. For example, a learner who struggles with grammar may choose grammar videos and quizzes. Teachers benefit too. The project introduces them to new methods and techniques, helps them grow professionally and builds their confidence with digital tools in class. The platforms also let them look up extra materials and check how well their students are progressing. Behind all of this is a clear aim: a better quality of education and a fair chance to succeed for every student. By putting technology in the classroom, Türkiye hopes to prepare young people for the future and to help teachers give lessons that work better.",
